      "writtenOn": "2020-04-20T17:01:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m concerned about using \u0027crypto_key_slot \u003d\u003d - 1\u0027 to represent that an mmc_request has crypto disabled, because there seem to be cases that initialize a \u0027struct mmc_request\u0027 to 0 without going through mmc_blk_data_prep().  For example, mmc_blk_cqe_prep_dcmd(), mmc_wait_for_cmd(),  __mmc_blk_ioctl_cmd(), and mmc_sd_num_wr_blocks().\n\nI think we should add a helper function that checks crypto_key instead:\n\n  #ifdef CONFIG_MMC_CRYPTO\n  static inline bool mmc_request_crypto_enabled(const struct mmc_request *mrq)\n  {\n          return mrq-\u003ecrypto_key !\u003d NULL;\n  }\n  #else\n  static inline bool mmc_request_crypto_enabled(const struct mmc_request *mrq)\n  {\n          return false;\n  }\n  #endif",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 166,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "369076766bf9b20b9718f238ee55dfa4ce2d3390",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59fcf793_31cbb6cc",
        "filename": "include/linux/mmc/core.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-20T17:07:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then mmc_crypto_prepare_req() could just do:\n\n        if (!bio_crypt_should_process(req)) \n                return;\n\n... since its caller initializes the mmc_request to 0.\n\nAnd in patches 2 and 3, cqhci_prep_crypto_desc() and msdc_prepare_crypto() would use mmc_request_crypto_enabled() instead of checking crypto_key_slot.\n\nA bool \u0027crypto_enabled\u0027 would also work, but since we already have \u0027crypto_key\u0027 we can use that.",
